      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Blocking issues must be resolved before approval.\n\n### Review Summary\n- **Functionality**: ✅ Pre-validating `rate` before locking `s-\u003emutex` and placing the FIFO into bypass mode prevents permanent mutex lockup on rejected rates, rejects negative and sub-minimum (`!rnd`) rates, avoids shift overflow on large rates, and unifies the register write path while only restarting the FIFO in stream mode when `rate \u003e 0`.\n- **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit**: ✅ Validating ODR parameters before mutating hardware FIFO state or acquiring the sensor mutex aligns with the ChromiumOS EC motion sensor driver contract.\n- **Code Simplicity**: ✅ Unifying the `rate \u003d\u003d 0` and `rate \u003e 0` register write paths and removing the unreachable post-normalization bounds check keeps `set_data_rate()` minimal and linear.\n- **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability**: ✅ Uses existing driver constants and Zephyr/ChromiumOS EC idioms cleanly.\n- **Security**: ✅ Prevents signed bit-shift overflow in `LIS2DH_ODR_TO_REG()` / `LIS2DH_ODR_TO_NORMALIZE()` and mutex deadlock on out-of-range ODR inputs.\n- **Testing**: ❌ `test_lis2dh__set_data_rate` in `zephyr/test/drivers/lis2dh/src/test_common.c` calls `set_data_rate(acc, 0, 1)` with `rnd \u003d 1` on power-off (which short-circuits `!rnd` on line 292 so `rate \u003e 0` is not tested at `rate \u003d\u003d 0`), omits the lower sub-minimum boundary `{ 1, 0 }` and `{ LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL + 1, 0 }`, and does not assert that the FIFO remains disabled (`!lis2dh_emul_is_fifo_enabled(emul)`) when powered off (`rate \u003d\u003d 0`).\n- **CL Size \u0026 Scope**: ✅ `Size: M (+58, -25)` — Single cohesive bug fix in `driver/accel_lis2dh.c` (+17, -25 lines) paired with its unit test updates in `zephyr/test/drivers/lis2dh/src/test_common.c` (+41 lines).\n- **Commit Message**: ✅ Clear, concise 3-paragraph prose description accurately documenting the problem, fix, and boundary behavior changes with `BUG\u003d` and `TEST\u003d` tags.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/99622247-b9a1-4476-a194-59410a43d7b2)",
