      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Add coverage for the remaining boundary conditions and the power-off FIFO state in `test_lis2dh__set_data_rate`:\n\n1. **`rate \u003e 0` boundary when `rnd \u003d\u003d 0` (`rate \u003d 0` and `rate \u003d 1`):** Calling `set_data_rate(acc, 0, 1)` on line 166 passes `rnd \u003d 1`, which short-circuits `!rnd` in `(!rnd \u0026\u0026 rate \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 rate \u003c LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL)` so `rate \u003e 0` is never evaluated at `rate \u003d\u003d 0` (even though `motion_sense_set_data_rate()` passes `rnd \u003d 0` when powering off). Likewise, `invalid[]` only checks the upper end of the sub-minimum range (`LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL - 1`), omitting the lower off-by-one boundary `{ 1, 0 }`.\n2. **Above-maximum rate with `rnd \u003d\u003d 0` (`{ LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL + 1, 0 }`):** As noted in the commit message, requests between the maximum and twice the maximum with `rnd \u003d\u003d 0` previously clamped to `LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL`, whereas `invalid[]` only tests `LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL + 1` with `rnd \u003d 1`.\n3. **FIFO disabled on power-off (`rate \u003d\u003d 0`):** Line 335 of `driver/accel_lis2dh.c` guards the stream-mode FIFO restart with `\u0026\u0026 rate \u003e 0`, but lines 165–167 do not verify that the FIFO stays in bypass mode (`!lis2dh_emul_is_fifo_enabled(emul)`) after powering off.\n\n```c\n\tconst struct {\n\t\tint rate;\n\t\tint rnd;\n\t} invalid[] \u003d {\n\t\t{ -1, 0 },\n\t\t{ LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL + 1, 0 },\n\t\t{ LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL + 1, 1 },\n\t\t{ INT_MAX, 1 },\n\t\t/* Below the minimum rate cannot be rounded down. */\n\t\t{ 1, 0 },\n\t\t{ LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL - 1, 0 },\n\t};\n```\n\nAnd in the power-off check on lines 165–167:\n\n```c\n\t/* Set data rate to 0 (Power Off) */\n\tzassert_ok(acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_data_rate(acc, 0, 0));\n\tzassert_equal(drvdata-\u003ebase.odr, 0);\n\tif (IS_ENABLED(ACCEL_LIS2DH_INT_ENABLE)) {\n\t\tzassert_false(lis2dh_emul_is_fifo_enabled(emul));\n\t}\n```\n\n- **Lines 165–167**: Power-off (`